hey guys Sean McGinnis here and I've  just spent a little over an hour messing  around with watchdogs  I say messing around because we've seen  a lot of the story missions so far but  this was really our first chance to just  wander around and explore the world  without any limitations now there are  two ways to do that  you either stroll around like some  average Joe or you pull out your phone  and explore Chicago like a badass hacker  this is when the city really comes to  life because everyone you pass by can be  profiled by a smart phone hacking  professions salaries web browsing habits  you name it you can even eavesdrop on  phone calls and read their text messages  it's a nice little touch to add some  real character to the city but it's not  just for show you might be able to hack  somebody's bank account and withdraw  their money from an ATM other times you  can find likely criminals and tail them  for a little street justice now like a  lot of you v Montreal games watchdogs is  very complex when it comes to just how  many gameplay systems that uses take  hacking for example there are CTOs  watchtowers that you can tap into in  order to unlock new hacking  opportunities on the map a bit like the  towers and Assassin's Creed as well as  an entire skill tree to learn new  abilities of course abilities require  skill points and that means doing  missions there's an entire stealth  system that plays a lot like Splinter  Cell or you can just run around with  guns blazing if that's what you prefer  personally I prefer watchdog stealth the  gunplay feels good but there's just so  much you can do in terms of hacking all  these different objects in the  environment plus if you want to spice  things up you can always steal cars and  get into a massive police chase  hopefully that gives you a little taste  of what it's like to play watchdogs if  you want even more information be sure  to check out my lengthy hands-on preview  on GameSpot calm
 

